  "order": 1,
  "maintainers": ["RadeenXALNW"],
  "units": "m",
  "description": "Interactive 3D figure for keeping left and right in a mirror, book page 234, topic 8.8.1, next to চিত্র ৮.২৬, and the উদাহরণ on page 223 (চিত্র ৮.১৫). A realistic boy holds up a card reading বাম in his left hand before two silvered-glass mirrors on a hinge. In one flat mirror the image raises its right hand and the writing is reversed. The student folds the mirrors to 90° and three images appear, each exact, seen only through the mirrors' own frames: the two reflected once stay swapped, and the corner image, reflected twice, keeps left as left and the writing reads true. Then the book's plan: a left fist in AOB, its ghosts in A′OB, AOB′ and A′OB′, and one ray traced from the hand by both mirrors to the eye. Five test questions. Offline, Bangla and English.",
